<speak>
<s>From <phoneme alphabet="ipa" ph="zʊhd">zuhd</phoneme> news, this is your briefing for <say-as interpret-as="date" format="dmy">14032026</say-as>.</s>
<break time="1s"/>
<s>Three point two million Iranians have fled their homes in twenty-two days — a pace of displacement matched only by Syria in 2011 — as United States and Israeli forces struck central Baghdad for the first time since the war began, killing a senior <phoneme alphabet="ipa" ph="kɑˈteɪb">Kataeb</phoneme> Hezbollah commander inside the Iraqi capital.</s> <s>Two thousand Marines have simultaneously left their Okinawa base for the Persian Gulf, stripping the Pacific of its only rapid-reaction force and leaving Japan and Taiwan less defended than at any point in recent years.</s> <s>The war is now in its twenty-second day, it is spreading onto a third country's soil, and no ceasefire talks are under way.</s>
<break time="900ms"/>
<s>In politics.</s><break time="400ms"/>
<s>A missile struck the United States embassy helipad in Baghdad — the first direct attack on American diplomatic soil since the war began on the twenty-eighth of February.</s> <s>Iraqi officials confirmed the strike; no armed group has claimed responsibility, and Washington has not announced any response.</s> <s>Iraq did not authorise the strikes that brought this war onto its territory, and it is now absorbing consequences it did not choose.</s>
<break time="600ms"/>
<s>Myanmar's military-backed party swept eighty percent of parliamentary seats in the country's first election since the 2021 coup, though it won only forty-four percent of the popular vote.</s> <s>A winner-takes-all electoral system inflated the result; opposition parties were banned from standing, and millions of displaced Burmese could not cast ballots.</s> <s>Parliament convenes next week with no international observers present and no opposition inside the chamber.</s>
<break time="600ms"/>
<s>Pakistan struck Kabul directly this week, destroying the three-thirteen Corps headquarters of Afghanistan's Taliban government, accusing it of sheltering the armed group behind most attacks on Pakistani soil.</s> <s>The Taliban retaliated by launching three drones toward Pakistani positions; Islamabad's military intercepted all three, though four people were wounded, including two children.</s> <s>Both sides say their operations will continue, and the exchange of airstrikes and drones across an international border marks a new and more dangerous phase of a conflict that has festered for years.</s>
<break time="600ms"/>
<s>Israel's National Security Minister <phoneme alphabet="ipa" ph="ˈɪtəmɑr bɛnˈɡvɪr">Itamar Ben-Gvir</phoneme> personally directed the live-broadcast arrest of <phoneme alphabet="ipa" ph="moˈhæmɪd sækæˈlɑ">Mohammed Sakallah</phoneme>, twenty-seven, for painting a Palestinian flag on a wall — charging him as a foreign agent.</s> <s>A court called the accusation weak, bordering on negligible, and ordered his release within hours.</s> <s>The minister staged the arrest in real time for a national audience, and the episode illustrates how public spectacle has become an instrument of political power.</s>
<break time="600ms"/>
<s>In the United States state of Michigan, a man drove a truck into a synagogue and died in a gunfight with police.</s> <s>The attacker, <phoneme alphabet="ipa" ph="ˈaɪmæn ɡæˈzɑli">Ayman Ghazali</phoneme>, had lost four relatives to Israeli airstrikes on Lebanon in the weeks before the attack; the Federal Bureau of Investigation is treating it as a targeted attack on the Jewish community but has not established a motive.</s> <s>His path from grief to violence is a reminder of how distant wars travel.</s>
<break time="900ms"/>
<s>On the economy.</s><break time="400ms"/>
<s>Shipping companies have imposed a three thousand dollar surcharge on every container bound for a Yemeni port — on ports far from the fighting — in a country that imports ninety percent of its food.</s> <s>Yemen's transport minister refused to pay and demanded the fees be reversed, but not one shipping company has complied.</s> <s>These costs do not fall on the carriers; they fall on Yemeni households, in a country already standing at the edge of famine.</s>
<break time="600ms"/>
<s>Brent crude closed the week at one hundred and one dollars a barrel — its first triple-digit price in years — after Iranian vessels struck two fuel tankers in Gulf waters on Thursday and shut down a major regional oil port entirely.</s> <s>A United States waiver on Russian oil purchases and the release of four hundred million barrels from emergency reserves failed to offset the Hormuz disruption.</s> <s>Washington has bombed infrastructure surrounding <phoneme alphabet="ipa" ph="kɑrɡ">Kharg</phoneme> Island — which handles over ninety percent of Iran's oil exports — but has spared the terminals themselves, holding them as leverage.</s>
<break time="600ms"/>
<s>Japan, France, and Canada are building a rare-earth supply network designed to free them from dependence on both Beijing and Washington.</s> <s>China controls over ninety percent of global rare-earth production, and American trade reversals under the Trump administration have left allies wary of exchanging one form of dependence for another.</s> <s>Canada is leading the initiative, which could, God willing, reshape the supply chains behind electric vehicles, semiconductors, and modern defence systems.</s>
<break time="900ms"/>
<s>In science.</s><break time="400ms"/>
<s>China's fifteenth five-year plan, released during the Two Sessions this month, sets no absolute limit on the country's carbon emissions — only a target tied to emissions per unit of economic output.</s> <s>Because China's economy is forecast to grow, analysts project that total emissions could still rise by three to six percent over the plan's five-year span, even if the per-unit target is met.</s> <s>The plan promotes gradual reductions in coal and oil consumption but offers no timeline, falling short of what climate scientists say is required to hold warming below one-and-a-half degrees Celsius.</s>
<break time="900ms"/>
<s>In technology.</s><break time="400ms"/>
<s>An eleven-year Cambridge University study found that Bitcoin's network could survive seventy-two percent of the world's submarine cables being severed — but that just five cloud-hosting providers run enough network nodes that targeting them could cripple the entire system.</s> <s>Bitcoin was designed to be decentralized, yet its practical infrastructure has quietly concentrated inside a handful of data centers.</s> <s>Node operators are now under pressure to diversify their hosting before the vulnerability is exploited.</s>
<break time="600ms"/>
<s>Anthropic's Claude artificial intelligence models can now process one million tokens — roughly seven hundred thousand words — in a single session, at no added cost for subscribers on paid plans.</s> <s>In independent benchmarks, the flagship Opus model recorded the highest long-context recall accuracy among frontier artificial intelligence systems, at seventy-eight point three percent.</s> <s>The capability raises a question the field has not yet answered: what does it mean to understand a document when a machine can hold an entire library in working memory at once.</s>
<break time="1s"/>
<s>That's your briefing from <phoneme alphabet="ipa" ph="zʊhd">zuhd</phoneme> news.</s>
</speak>